**Issue**: #274
**Date**: 2026-08-26
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-274 @bug @execute @review-picker
Feature: Navigate paginated wrapped review branch picker
  As a Herdr operator running nmg-sdlc execute
  I want review workers to select the default branch through paginated picker output
  So that long branch lists do not stop delivery before project-aware review begins

  Background:
    Given the repository default branch is "main"
    And the known Git branch list contains 18 ordered branches

  Scenario: Complete visible page is accepted with main off-screen
    Given OMP renders the first five branch options
    And long visible branch names wrap across terminal lines
    And the picker shows "(1/18) Type to search"
    And exactly one visible option owns the cursor
    And "main" is not visible
    When execute observes the review branch picker
    Then the visible fragments reconstruct to one contiguous known-branch segment
    And the picker is recognized as complete

  Scenario: Default branch is selected across the page boundary
    Given the recognized cursor branch precedes "main" in the known branch order
    When execute drives the review selection
    Then it sends one Down event per intervening branch index
    And it appends Enter
    And it waits for the review worker to start and settle
    And only then submits the project-aware review worker prompt

  Scenario: Selection after main navigates upward without wraparound
    Given the recognized cursor branch follows "main" in the known branch order
    When execute drives the review selection
    Then it sends one Up event per intervening branch index
    And it appends Enter

  Scenario Outline: Unsafe picker output fails closed
    Given the terminal picker output is <condition>
    When execute observes the review branch picker
    Then it sends no branch-selection keys
    And the review step stops with reason "review_failed"

    Examples:
      | condition                                      |
      | partial before its navigation footer renders  |
      | malformed against known branch names          |
      | missing a cursor                               |
      | containing multiple cursors                    |
      | ambiguous across known contiguous segments     |
      | unrelated terminal content                     |

  Scenario Outline: Existing review lifecycle remains supported
    Given a <worker> review worker renders a <layout> picker
    When execute selects the default branch
    Then review orchestration continues through the existing handoff boundary

    Examples:
      | worker   | layout              |
      | fresh    | numbered            |
      | fresh    | unnumbered          |
      | fresh    | wrapped unnumbered  |
      | retained | numbered            |
      | retained | wrapped unnumbered  |
      | retained | paginated wrapped   |
